  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>No two pages of this book are in the same hand. The ink is still wet on the last page however long the book has been closed, and the last page is never the same one.</p><p>While you hold this book, you can use it as a Spellcasting Focus, and you have a +3 bonus to spell attack rolls and to the saving throw DCs of your spells.</p><p><strong>Borrowed Hand.</strong> Once per day, you can cast any spell of level 5 or lower from any class's spell list, reading it from the codex. You expend no spell slot and need no Material components. The codex regains this power at dawn.</p><p><strong>A Thousand Hands.</strong> Every scribe who ever copied a page of the codex left their handwriting in it, and their knowledge with it. Once per week the reader can ask the book a question of lore, and one of the thousand answers in the margin, in their own hand and with their own opinions.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
